  m_Name: ScrewTypeCompressorData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  engineName: Screw Type Compressor
  engineDescription: A Screw Compressor is a positive-displacement compressor used
    for continuously compressing gases, particularly air and refrigerants, by trapping
    and reducing the volume of gas between intermeshing helical rotors. Its main
    components include the casing, male rotor, female rotor, inlet port, discharge
    port, bearings, shaft, seals, and lubrication system. During operation, gas enters
    through the inlet and is trapped between the rotating screw profiles and the
    casing. As the rotors rotate, the trapped gas is carried along the length of
    the rotors while the available volume gradually decreases, causing the gas pressure
    to increase. The compressed gas is then discharged through the outlet port. Screw
    compressors are widely used in industrial compressed-air systems, refrigeration
    and air-conditioning equipment, chemical processing, gas handling, and manufacturing
    plants. From an engineering perspective, understanding rotor geometry, compression
    ratio, volumetric efficiency, oil injection, sealing, lubrication, heat generation,
    leakage, vibration, and maintenance is essential for ensuring efficient and reliable
    compressor performance.
  engineCategory: Engineering
